import Mathlib
import Conjectures.Goldbach.RoughFifthMass

/-!
Glue for L-twin-primes-cut-e341d9faa41cec93161bce4e.

Part A: the e724 definitions and its count (proved by the e724 assembly).
Part B: the rough upper bound, copied from the accepted cut
        Conjectures.Cuts.Refute359fb2bfba7687230b3e5a26 (reverse_rough_upper_unconditional and
        everything it needs).
Part C: the glue: the eighth-root reverse Chen set sits inside the good part of the published
        rough set (adapted from reverseChen_set_subset_good_rough of the same accepted cut), and
        the count plus the upper bound give the published bad-fraction bound (adapted from
        e341_frozen_of_reverse_P2_and_rough_upper of the same accepted cut).
-/


/-!
Blueprint v3 for the twin-prime cut e724 (Chen, reverse shift, Selberg-weighted form).

Route (Tao, 254A Supplement 5, section 3, with the shift reversed; Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_z = x^(1/8)).

The published sum is supported on n prime, weight (log n)^2, and on n = p*q with p != q
prime, weight 2 log p log q. So it is enough to count, for large x, the set of n <= x with
n + 2 prime that are prime or a product of two distinct primes, all prime factors being at
least x^(1/8). The count is obtained from the three sieve terms of Chen's argument, with
explicit constants:

  A1  (lower Rosser sieve, s -> 4)                      coefficient Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_a1 = f(4 - 8 eps)
  A2  (upper Rosser sieve per prime p in [Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_z, x^(1/3)])  coefficient Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_a2 = int F(4 - 8 eps - t) dt/t
  A3  (switched upper sieve on p1 p2 p3 + 2 at s = 3/2) coefficient Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_b3 = F(3/2) times Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_V(Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_w) / Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_V(Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_z)

The switched term needs the Bombieri-Vinogradov theorem for the convolution of a bounded
sequence with primes in a short interval (Tao, Notes 3, Theorem 16). That theorem is built
here from the bilinear large sieve and Siegel-Walfisz of Conjectures.Goldbach.RoughFifthMass
in five steps (Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_conv_class_le, Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_conv_induced_le, Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_conv_char_reduce, Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_conv_block_bilinear,
Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_conv_block_small, Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_prime_interval_sw, Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_conv_bv). The Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_level is sqrt(x)/(log x)^100, which is
what the block sum R sqrt(x) allows; eps = 1/1000 is the Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_slack kept in the constants.

Helpers, in dependency order:

  Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_conv_class_le        discrepancy in one class <= non-principal character mean (orthogonality)
  Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_conv_induced_le      characters mod q -> primitive characters of the conductors r | q, r > 1
  Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_conv_char_reduce     sum over q <= Q of the character means <= (1 + log Q)^2 times the
                       primitive-conductor majorant
  Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_conv_block_bilinear  one dyadic block of conductors, by the bilinear large sieve
  Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_conv_block_small     one dyadic block of small conductors, by the large sieve for one factor
                       and Siegel-Walfisz for the prime factor
  Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_prime_interval_sw    Siegel-Walfisz for primes in [L, U] with U <= L (1 + log^-20 x)
  Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_conv_bv              the convolution Bombieri-Vinogradov at Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_level sqrt(x)/log^100 x

  Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_chen_numeric         the constants: the Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_triple integral Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_C <= 3631/10000 and the comparison
                       8 (1 - eps)^3 Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_a1 - 4 (1 + eps)^2 Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_a2 - (3/2)(1 + eps)^3 Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_b3 Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_C/(1 - 2 eps) >= 1/100
  Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_chen_V_bounds        Mertens for Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_V(y) = prod_{3 <= p < y} (1 - 1/(p-1)) at y = Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_z and y = Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_w
  Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_chen_A1_lower        lower sieve count of the Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_z-Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_rough n in (x/2, x] with n + 2 prime
  Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_chen_A2_upper        sum over p in [Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_z, x^(1/3)] of the same set with p | n
  Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_chen_triple_size     number of p1 p2 p3 in (x/2, x] with Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_z <= p1 <= x^(1/3) < p2 <= p3
  Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_chen_triple_switch   switched upper sieve: among those, the ones with n + 2 prime
  Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_chen_weight_sum      Chen's pointwise weight (Tao, Lemma 11), summed over the Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_rough set
-/

section
open scoped BigOperators
open Classical
open Filter


/-! ### Constants and parameters -/

/-- The fixed Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_slack eps0 = 1/1000. -/
noncomputable def Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_slack : ℝ := 1 / 1000

/-- The lower sieve factor f(4 - 8 eps) = 2 e^gamma log(3 - 8 eps)/(4 - 8 eps). -/
noncomputable def Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_a1 : ℝ :=
  2 * Real.exp Real.eulerMascheroniConstant * Real.log (3 - 8 * Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_slack) / (4 - 8 * Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_slack)

/-- The upper sieve sum int_1^{8/3} F(4 - 8 eps - t) dt/t. -/
noncomputable def Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_a2 : ℝ :=
  2 * Real.exp Real.eulerMascheroniConstant *
    Real.log ((8 / 3) * (3 - 8 * Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_slack) / (4 / 3 - 8 * Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_slack)) / (4 - 8 * Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_slack)

/-- The switched upper sieve factor F(3/2) = 4 e^gamma / 3. -/
noncomputable def Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_b3 : ℝ := 4 * Real.exp Real.eulerMascheroniConstant / 3

/-- The eighth-Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_root cutoff Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_z = ceil(x^(1/8)). -/
noncomputable def Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_z (x : ℕ) : ℕ := ⌈(x : ℝ) ^ (1 / 8 : ℝ)⌉₊

/-- The cube-Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_root cutoff floor(x^(1/3)). -/
noncomputable def Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_root (x : ℕ) : ℕ := ⌊(x : ℝ) ^ (1 / 3 : ℝ)⌋₊

/-- The Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_level of distribution D = sqrt(x)/(log x)^100. -/
noncomputable def Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_level (x : ℕ) : ℕ :=
  ⌊(x : ℝ) ^ (1 / 2 : ℝ) / (Real.log (x : ℝ)) ^ (100 : ℕ)⌋₊

/-- The switched sifting Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_level Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_w = ceil(D^(2/3)), so that log D / log Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_w = 3/2. -/
noncomputable def Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_w (x : ℕ) : ℕ := ⌈((Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_level x : ℝ)) ^ (2 / 3 : ℝ)⌉₊

/-- The sieve density Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_V(y) = prod_{3 <= p < y} (1 - 1/(p - 1)) of the reversed shift. -/
noncomputable def Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_V (y : ℕ) : ℝ :=
  ∏ p ∈ (Finset.Icc 3 (y - 1)).filter Nat.Prime, (1 - 1 / ((p : ℝ) - 1))

/-- The Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_triple integral of Chen's A3 term, in its one-dimensional form. -/
noncomputable def Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_C : ℝ :=
  ∫ t in (1 / 8 : ℝ)..(1 / 3 : ℝ), Real.log (2 - 3 * t) / (t * (1 - t))

/-! ### The sets of Chen's argument -/

/-- The Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_z-Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_rough candidates: n in (x/2, x] with n + 2 prime and every prime factor of n
at least Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_z. -/
noncomputable def Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_rough (x : ℕ) : Finset ℕ :=
  (Finset.Ioc (x / 2) x).filter fun n =>
    (n + 2).Prime ∧ ∀ p ∈ n.primeFactors, Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_z x ≤ p

/-- The candidates that are a prime or a product of two distinct primes. -/
noncomputable def Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_good (x : ℕ) : Finset ℕ :=
  (Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_rough x).filter fun n =>
    n.Prime ∨ ∃ p q : ℕ, p.Prime ∧ q.Prime ∧ p ≠ q ∧ n = p * q

/-- The candidates divisible by p. -/
noncomputable def Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_shifted (x p : ℕ) : Finset ℕ :=
  (Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_rough x).filter fun n => p ∣ n

/-- The triples p1 p2 p3 in (x/2, x] with Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_z <= p1 <= x^(1/3) < p2 <= p3. -/
noncomputable def Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_tripleRaw (x : ℕ) : Finset ℕ :=
  (Finset.Ioc (x / 2) x).filter fun n =>
    ∃ p1 p2 p3 : ℕ, p1.Prime ∧ p2.Prime ∧ p3.Prime ∧ Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_z x ≤ p1 ∧ p1 ≤ Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_root x ∧
      Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_root x < p2 ∧ p2 ≤ p3 ∧ n = p1 * p2 * p3

/-- The triples whose shift is prime. -/
noncomputable def Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_triple (x : ℕ) : Finset ℕ :=
  (Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_tripleRaw x).filter fun n => (n + 2).Prime

/-! ### The convolution Bombieri-Vinogradov theorem -/

/-- Character sum of the part of `a` supported on `Icc 1 M` that is coprime to `s`. -/
noncomputable def Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_coprimeSum (a : ℕ → ℝ) (M s r : ℕ) (χ : DirichletCharacter ℂ r) : ℂ :=
  ∑ m ∈ Finset.Icc 1 M, (a m : ℂ) * (if Nat.Coprime m s then 1 else 0) * χ (m : ZMod r)

/-- The convolution of `α` on `Icc 1 M` and `β` on `Icc 1 N`. -/
noncomputable def Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_convSeq (α β : ℕ → ℝ) (M N n : ℕ) : ℝ :=
  ∑ m ∈ Finset.Icc 1 M, ∑ k ∈ Finset.Icc 1 N, if m * k = n then α m * β k else 0

/-- Discrepancy of the convolution in the residue class `c` modulo `q`. -/
noncomputable def Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_convDelta (α β : ℕ → ℝ) (M N q c : ℕ) : ℝ :=
  (∑ n ∈ (Finset.Icc 1 (M * N)).filter (fun n => n % q = c % q), Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_convSeq α β M N n) -
    (1 / (q.totient : ℝ)) *
      ∑ n ∈ (Finset.Icc 1 (M * N)).filter (fun n => Nat.Coprime n q), Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_convSeq α β M N n

/-- Primitive-character mass of the `s`-coprime parts of `α` and `β`. -/
noncomputable def Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_nonprincipal (q : ℕ) :
    Finset (DirichletCharacter ℂ q) := by
  classical
  exact @Finset.erase (DirichletCharacter ℂ q) (fun a b => Classical.propDecidable (a = b))
    (Finset.univ : Finset (DirichletCharacter ℂ q)) 1

noncomputable def Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_primChars (r : ℕ) :
    Finset (DirichletCharacter ℂ r) := by
  classical
  exact @Finset.filter (DirichletCharacter ℂ r) (fun χ => χ.IsPrimitive)
    (fun χ => Classical.propDecidable (χ.IsPrimitive))
    (Finset.univ : Finset (DirichletCharacter ℂ r))

noncomputable def Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_primMass (α β : ℕ → ℝ) (M N s r : ℕ) : ℝ :=
  ∑ χ ∈ Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_primChars r,
    ‖Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_coprimeSum α M s r χ * Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_coprimeSum β N s r χ‖

/-- Indicator of the primes of the interval `Icc L U`. -/
noncomputable def Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_primeInd (L U : ℕ) : ℕ → ℝ :=
  fun n => if L ≤ n ∧ n ≤ U ∧ n.Prime then 1 else 0

-- @helper Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_conv_class_le
/-- Character expansion: the discrepancy of the convolution in a reduced class is bounded by the
mean over the non-principal characters. -/
theorem Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_conv_class_le (α β : ℕ → ℝ) (M N q c : ℕ)
    (hq : 1 ≤ q) (hc : c < q) (hcop : Nat.Coprime c q) :
    |Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_convDelta α β M N q c| ≤
      (1 / (q.totient : ℝ)) *
        ∑ χ ∈ Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_nonprincipal q,
          ‖∑ n ∈ Finset.Icc 1 (M * N),
            (Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_convSeq α β M N n : ℂ) * χ (n : ZMod q)‖ := by
  classical
  have hq0 : NeZero q := ⟨by omega⟩
  have hcu : IsUnit (c : ZMod q) := (ZMod.isUnit_iff_coprime c q).mpr hcop
  set a : ℕ → ℝ := fun n => Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_convSeq α β M N n
  have hiff : ∀ n : ℕ, ((c : ZMod q) = (n : ZMod q)) ↔ n % q = c % q := by
    intro n
    constructor
    · intro h
      have h' := congrArg (ZMod.val (n := q)) h
      simpa [ZMod.val_natCast, Nat.mod_eq_of_lt hc] using h'.symm
    · intro h
      apply ZMod.val_injective
      simpa [ZMod.val_natCast, Nat.mod_eq_of_lt hc] using h.symm
  have horth : (∑ χ : DirichletCharacter ℂ q, χ ((c : ZMod q)⁻¹) *
        ∑ n ∈ Finset.Icc 1 (M * N), (a n : ℂ) * χ (n : ZMod q)) =
      (q.totient : ℂ) * ∑ n ∈ (Finset.Icc 1 (M * N)).filter (fun n => n % q = c % q), (a n : ℂ) := by
    have h1 : (∑ χ : DirichletCharacter ℂ q, χ ((c : ZMod q)⁻¹) *
          ∑ n ∈ Finset.Icc 1 (M * N), (a n : ℂ) * χ (n : ZMod q)) =
        ∑ n ∈ Finset.Icc 1 (M * N), (a n : ℂ) *
          (∑ χ : DirichletCharacter ℂ q, χ ((c : ZMod q)⁻¹) * χ (n : ZMod q)) := by
      simp_rw [Finset.mul_sum]
      rw [Finset.sum_comm]
      refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun n _ => ?_
      refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun χ _ => ?_
      ring
    rw [h1]
    have h2 : ∀ n : ℕ, (∑ χ : DirichletCharacter ℂ q, χ ((c : ZMod q)⁻¹) * χ (n : ZMod q)) =
        if (c : ZMod q) = (n : ZMod q) then (q.totient : ℂ) else 0 :=
      fun n => DirichletCharacter.sum_char_inv_mul_char_eq ℂ hcu (n : ZMod q)
    simp_rw [h2, hiff]
    rw [Finset.sum_filter, Finset.mul_sum]
    refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun n _ => ?_
    split_ifs <;> ring
  have hone : (∑ n ∈ Finset.Icc 1 (M * N), (a n : ℂ) * (1 : DirichletCharacter ℂ q) (n : ZMod q)) =
      ∑ n ∈ (Finset.Icc 1 (M * N)).filter (fun n => Nat.Coprime n q), (a n : ℂ) := by
    have h1 : ∀ n : ℕ, (1 : DirichletCharacter ℂ q) (n : ZMod q) =
        if IsUnit (n : ZMod q) then 1 else 0 := by
      intro n
      by_cases h : IsUnit (n : ZMod q)
      · rw [if_pos h, MulChar.one_apply h]
      · rw [if_neg h, MulChar.map_nonunit _ h]
    simp_rw [h1, ZMod.isUnit_iff_coprime]
    rw [Finset.sum_filter]
    refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun n _ => ?_
    split_ifs <;> ring
  have h3 : (∑ χ ∈ Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_nonprincipal q,
        χ ((c : ZMod q)⁻¹) * ∑ n ∈ Finset.Icc 1 (M * N), (a n : ℂ) * χ (n : ZMod q)) =
      (∑ χ : DirichletCharacter ℂ q, χ ((c : ZMod q)⁻¹) *
        ∑ n ∈ Finset.Icc 1 (M * N), (a n : ℂ) * χ (n : ZMod q)) -
      ∑ n ∈ Finset.Icc 1 (M * N), (a n : ℂ) * (1 : DirichletCharacter ℂ q) (n : ZMod q) := by
    have hcu' : IsUnit ((c : ZMod q)⁻¹) := by
      have hc' : (c : ZMod q) = (hcu.unit : ZMod q) := hcu.unit_spec.symm
      rw [hc', ZMod.inv_coe_unit]
      exact (hcu.unit⁻¹).isUnit
    have h : (∑ χ ∈ Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_nonprincipal q,
        χ ((c : ZMod q)⁻¹) * ∑ n ∈ Finset.Icc 1 (M * N), (a n : ℂ) * χ (n : ZMod q)) +
        ∑ n ∈ Finset.Icc 1 (M * N), (a n : ℂ) * (1 : DirichletCharacter ℂ q) (n : ZMod q) =
      (∑ χ : DirichletCharacter ℂ q, χ ((c : ZMod q)⁻¹) *
        ∑ n ∈ Finset.Icc 1 (M * N), (a n : ℂ) * χ (n : ZMod q)) := by
      have h0 := @Finset.sum_erase_add (DirichletCharacter ℂ q) ℂ _
        (fun a b => Classical.propDecidable (a = b)) Finset.univ
        (fun χ : DirichletCharacter ℂ q => χ ((c : ZMod q)⁻¹) *
          ∑ n ∈ Finset.Icc 1 (M * N), (a n : ℂ) * χ (n : ZMod q)) 1 (Finset.mem_univ 1)
      rw [MulChar.one_apply hcu', one_mul] at h0
      unfold Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_nonprincipal
      exact h0
    rw [← h]
    ring
  have hmain : ((Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_convDelta α β M N q c : ℝ) : ℂ) =
      (1 / (q.totient : ℂ)) *
        ∑ χ ∈ Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_nonprincipal q,
          χ ((c : ZMod q)⁻¹) * ∑ n ∈ Finset.Icc 1 (M * N), (a n : ℂ) * χ (n : ZMod q) := by
    have hΔ : ((Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_convDelta α β M N q c : ℝ) : ℂ) =
        (∑ n ∈ (Finset.Icc 1 (M * N)).filter (fun n => n % q = c % q), (a n : ℂ)) -
        (1 / (q.totient : ℂ)) *
          ∑ n ∈ (Finset.Icc 1 (M * N)).filter (fun n => Nat.Coprime n q), (a n : ℂ) := by
      unfold Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_convDelta
      push_cast
      ring
    rw [hΔ, h3, horth, hone]
    have hφ : (q.totient : ℂ) ≠ 0 := by exact_mod_cast (Nat.totient_pos.mpr hq).ne'
    field_simp
  have hnorm : |Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_convDelta α β M N q c| =
      ‖((Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_convDelta α β M N q c : ℝ) : ℂ)‖ :=
    (Complex.norm_real _).symm
  rw [hnorm, hmain]
  refine le_trans (norm_mul_le _ _) ?_
  have hnn : ‖(1 / (q.totient : ℂ))‖ = 1 / (q.totient : ℝ) := by
    rw [norm_div, norm_one, Complex.norm_natCast]
  rw [hnn]
  refine mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left ?_ (by positivity)
  refine le_trans (norm_sum_le _ _) ?_
  refine Finset.sum_le_sum fun χ _ => ?_
  rw [norm_mul]
  have hχ := DirichletCharacter.norm_le_one χ ((c : ZMod q)⁻¹)
  have hpos : 0 ≤ ‖∑ n ∈ Finset.Icc 1 (M * N), (a n : ℂ) * χ (n : ZMod q)‖ := norm_nonneg _
  nlinarith

-- @end Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_conv_class_le

-- @helper Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_conv_induced_le
/-- A character modulo `q` is its primitive character of conductor `r` times the coprimality
factor 1_{(n, q/r) = 1}, and the convolution then factorises. -/
theorem Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_conv_induced_le (α β : ℕ → ℝ) (M N q : ℕ) (hq : 1 ≤ q) :
    (∑ χ ∈ Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_nonprincipal q,
        ‖∑ n ∈ Finset.Icc 1 (M * N),
          (Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_convSeq α β M N n : ℂ) * χ (n : ZMod q)‖) ≤
      ∑ r ∈ (q.divisors).filter (fun r => 1 < r),
        Taske724d7d203de1af512de02c5_primMass α β M N (q / r) r := by
  classical
  haveI : NeZero q := ⟨by omega⟩
  have hkey : ∀ (χ : DirichletCharacter ℂ q) (n : ℕ),
      χ (n : ZMod q) = χ.primitiveCharacter (n : ZMod χ.conductor) *
        (if Nat.Coprime n (q / χ.conductor) then 1 else 0) := by
    intro χ n
    have hr : χ.conductor ∣ q := χ.conductor_dvd_level
    by_cases hn : Nat.Coprime n q
